WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.465
This repository is Odoo 20, narrowed

2
00:00:02.465 --> 00:00:04.931
to a practical problem: keeping a

3
00:00:04.931 --> 00:00:07.396
CRM pipeline useful when the network

4
00:00:07.396 --> 00:00:09.861
disappears. The desktop pipeline shows leads

5
00:00:09.861 --> 00:00:12.327
moving through New, Qualified, Proposition, and

6
00:00:12.327 --> 00:00:14.792
Won. The mobile capture shows the

7
00:00:14.792 --> 00:00:17.257
same work continuing offline. That path

8
00:00:17.257 --> 00:00:19.723
is the fork's center: CRM consumes

9
00:00:19.723 --> 00:00:22.188
an offline framework owned by the

10
00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.653
web client, instead of inventing a

11
00:00:24.653 --> 00:00:25.475
second one.

12
00:00:26.275 --> 00:00:29.182
The repository is a large Python

13
00:00:29.182 --> 00:00:32.090
application server surrounded by 642 addon

14
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:34.997
modules. The core reports version 20.0,

15
00:00:34.998 --> 00:00:37.905
Python 3.12 through 3.14, and PostgreSQL

16
00:00:37.905 --> 00:00:40.812
16 or newer. The tree includes

17
00:00:40.812 --> 00:00:42.266
accounting, sales, inventory,

18
00:00:42.266 --> 00:00:43.720
websites, human resources,

19
00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:46.628
point of sale, marketing, and 229

20
00:00:46.628 --> 00:00:49.535
country localizations. The useful mental model

21
00:00:49.535 --> 00:00:52.442
is one server, one module graph,

22
00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:55.350
and many applications extending shared models.

23
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.636
Start at odoo-bin. The CLI selects

24
00:00:58.636 --> 00:01:01.123
a command, then the server chooses

25
00:01:01.123 --> 00:01:03.609
a threaded, prefork, or gevent runtime.

26
00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:06.095
A database gets a registry. The

27
00:01:06.095 --> 00:01:08.582
module loader imports Python models and

28
00:01:08.582 --> 00:01:11.068
loads XML and CSV data in

29
00:01:11.068 --> 00:01:13.555
dependency order. An HTTP request resolves

30
00:01:13.555 --> 00:01:16.041
a session and database, matches a

31
00:01:16.041 --> 00:01:18.527
route, selects a dispatcher, and reaches

32
00:01:18.527 --> 00:01:21.014
a controller or model. SQL runs

33
00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.500
through the pooled PostgreSQL connection layer.

34
00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.865
The ORM is extracted under odoo/orm.

35
00:01:26.865 --> 00:01:29.430
Models operate on recordsets, fields declare

36
00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.995
the schema, and domains form an

37
00:01:31.995 --> 00:01:34.560
optimized search tree. A write first

38
00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.125
checks access and marks values in

39
00:01:37.125 --> 00:01:39.690
the transaction cache. SQL is flushed

40
00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:42.255
later in batches. Odoo 20 also

41
00:01:42.255 --> 00:01:44.820
unifies access rights and record rules

42
00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.385
in ir.access, so the same model

43
00:01:47.385 --> 00:01:49.950
layer handles business data and authorization.

44
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.678
crm.lead carries the pipeline. Its lifecycle

45
00:01:53.678 --> 00:01:55.142
covers leads and

46
00:01:55.142 --> 00:01:56.605
opportunities, stages, probability,

47
00:01:56.605 --> 00:01:59.533
won and lost transitions, contacts, expected

48
00:01:59.533 --> 00:02:02.461
revenue, and recurring revenue. Predictive Lead

49
00:02:02.461 --> 00:02:05.388
Scoring uses per-team won and lost

50
00:02:05.388 --> 00:02:06.852
frequencies to estimate

51
00:02:06.852 --> 00:02:08.316
automated probability. Teams

52
00:02:08.316 --> 00:02:11.244
can allocate leads with member quotas.

53
00:02:11.244 --> 00:02:14.171
Forecast views project prorated revenue, while

54
00:02:14.171 --> 00:02:17.099
merge and duplicate tools keep the

55
00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:18.075
pipeline usable.

56
00:02:18.875 --> 00:02:21.670
The browser client boots from main.js

57
00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:24.465
into start.js and WebClient. OWL 3

58
00:02:24.465 --> 00:02:27.260
is vendored behind a compatibility layer

59
00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:30.055
in a directory still named owl2.

60
00:02:30.055 --> 00:02:32.850
Core plugins provide RPC, ORM, errors,

61
00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.645
UI, dialogs, popovers, and registries. The

62
00:02:35.645 --> 00:02:38.440
relational model feeds form, list, kanban,

63
00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:41.235
calendar, graph, and pivot views. Addons

64
00:02:41.235 --> 00:02:44.030
customize those views through registry entries

65
00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.825
and the js_class attribute in XML.

66
00:02:47.625 --> 00:02:50.052
When a form save or list

67
00:02:50.052 --> 00:02:52.478
operation meets a lost connection, the

68
00:02:52.478 --> 00:02:54.905
relational model schedules the ORM call.

69
00:02:54.905 --> 00:02:57.331
The queue stores the model, method,

70
00:02:57.331 --> 00:02:58.545
arguments, keyword arguments,

71
00:02:58.545 --> 00:02:59.758
and display metadata

72
00:02:59.758 --> 00:03:02.185
in the orm-to-sync table. The offline

73
00:03:02.185 --> 00:03:04.611
systray shows the pending change. When

74
00:03:04.611 --> 00:03:07.038
the connection returns, a Web Lock

75
00:03:07.038 --> 00:03:09.465
serializes replay across tabs. Entries run

76
00:03:09.465 --> 00:03:11.891
in timestamp order, with a pause

77
00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:12.700
between calls.

78
00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.981
The offline database is wrapped by

79
00:03:15.981 --> 00:03:18.462
a per-tab mutex and versioned with

80
00:03:18.462 --> 00:03:20.943
the asset registry hash. When the

81
00:03:20.943 --> 00:03:23.424
registry changes, the store is invalidated

82
00:03:23.424 --> 00:03:25.905
rather than migrated. Values use AES-GCM

83
00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.386
with a fresh initialization vector. The

84
00:03:28.386 --> 00:03:30.867
browser secret comes from the session

85
00:03:30.867 --> 00:03:33.348
bootstrap and is derived server-side from

86
00:03:33.348 --> 00:03:35.829
session token fields, so changing a

87
00:03:35.829 --> 00:03:38.310
password or second factor rotates the

88
00:03:38.310 --> 00:03:39.550
local encryption key.

89
00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.913
One service worker serves the /odoo

90
00:03:42.913 --> 00:03:45.476
scope. It caches the homepage and

91
00:03:45.476 --> 00:03:48.039
offline page, uses network-first navigation, and

92
00:03:48.039 --> 00:03:50.602
masks session information before storing HTML.

93
00:03:50.602 --> 00:03:53.165
The PWA service captures the install

94
00:03:53.165 --> 00:03:55.728
prompt and supports scoped app manifests.

95
00:03:55.728 --> 00:03:58.291
CRM and account can enable the

96
00:03:58.291 --> 00:04:00.853
share target. CRM adds a team

97
00:04:00.853 --> 00:04:03.416
picker so a shared item can

98
00:04:03.416 --> 00:04:05.125
become a new lead.

99
00:04:05.925 --> 00:04:08.677
Small-screen behavior is driven by UIPlugin

100
00:04:08.677 --> 00:04:10.053
signals and matchMedia

101
00:04:10.053 --> 00:04:11.428
breakpoints. Bottom sheets

102
00:04:11.428 --> 00:04:14.180
replace floating popovers where the call

103
00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:16.932
site opts in. The CRM PLS

104
00:04:16.932 --> 00:04:19.684
tooltip is one example. Offline action

105
00:04:19.684 --> 00:04:22.435
helper screens let a user recover

106
00:04:22.435 --> 00:04:25.187
a view from remembered searches. The

107
00:04:25.187 --> 00:04:27.939
test wrapper runs the CRM JavaScript

108
00:04:27.939 --> 00:04:30.691
suite under desktop and a 375

109
00:04:30.691 --> 00:04:32.525
by 667 mobile preset.

110
00:04:33.325 --> 00:04:36.035
The development scripts exist because Odoo

111
00:04:36.035 --> 00:04:38.746
can report success while collecting zero

112
00:04:38.746 --> 00:04:41.456
tests or silently skipping browser tests.

113
00:04:41.456 --> 00:04:44.166
The wrappers choose install versus update

114
00:04:44.166 --> 00:04:46.877
correctly, update crm and web for

115
00:04:46.877 --> 00:04:49.587
JavaScript collection, and fail on empty

116
00:04:49.587 --> 00:04:50.942
selections. Frontend changes

117
00:04:50.942 --> 00:04:52.297
require asset regeneration.

118
00:04:52.297 --> 00:04:55.008
The normal check is Python, desktop

119
00:04:55.008 --> 00:04:57.718
JavaScript, mobile JavaScript, and the forbidden

120
00:04:57.718 --> 00:04:59.525
only or debug guard.

121
00:05:00.325 --> 00:05:02.573
To change this fork, start in

122
00:05:02.573 --> 00:05:04.821
addons/crm and follow the project rules

123
00:05:04.821 --> 00:05:07.069
in AGENTS.md. Use the web client

124
00:05:07.069 --> 00:05:09.317
as the extension point, not a

125
00:05:09.317 --> 00:05:11.565
parallel offline engine. Run the scripted

126
00:05:11.565 --> 00:05:13.813
tests in both viewport presets and

127
00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:16.062
report the results. The shortest route

128
00:05:16.062 --> 00:05:18.310
through the code is CRM models,

129
00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:20.558
CRM views, the relational model, and

130
00:05:20.558 --> 00:05:22.806
OfflinePlugin. That is the shape of

131
00:05:22.806 --> 00:05:25.054
Odoo here: a broad ERP core,

132
00:05:25.054 --> 00:05:27.302
focused CRM work, and offline behavior

133
00:05:27.302 --> 00:05:29.550
owned by the shared web layer.

